From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?=C3=98yvind=20Harboe?= <oyvind.harboe@zylin.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 19:49:28 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] gpl: a waiting routability pass is not cancelled by
 convergence
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Routability-driven global placement runs its routability pass once the
average overflow is at or below routability_check_overflow (0.30 by
default) and the cells have settled: in every region, the displacement
per iteration is at or below 60% of its running peak. While the
overflow gate is open and the cells are still moving,
NesterovPlace::runRoutability logs GPL-0099 once and waits. The
convergence test that follows it in the same iteration does not look at
the wait: it ends the placement once every region's overflow is at or
below the target overflow (0.10 by default). A wait still open on that
iteration ends with the placement, and global placement finishes with
exit status 0 without the pending routability pass and without the
inflation it would have made. The log shows GPL-0099 and then the usual
end messages from GPL-1001 on, with no GPL-0103 and no GPL-0040 after
the GPL-0099.

On a large hierarchical design (XiangShan's XSTile parent, in
bazel-orfs), 1.8 million movable instances, the log has GPL-0099 at
iter = 474, with the cells at 83% of their peak displacement, and
GPL-1001 at iteration 550, converged at overflow 0.0936 with no pass
at all. A later build of that parent did the same: GPL-0099 at
iter = 438 at 91%, GPL-1001 at iteration 507, no pass. Another run of
the same design closed seven waits at overflows between 0.118 and
0.137, just above the target, so on a design of that size the race is
close.

A wait still open on the iteration the placement would converge now
ends there, and the pass runs on that placement. GPL-0124 says so, with
the overflow, the target and how fast the cells are still moving.
"Would converge" is NesterovBase::isConvergenceDue(), the test
checkConvergence() itself uses, asked of every region as isConverged()
asks it. A wait ends this way only when a routability snapshot is
saved, since the pass goes back to it when it finds congestion. When
that pass reverts, the previous change keeps the placement from
converging on the overflow of the placement it replaced, and it goes
down from the snapshot again.

What does not change: a design whose cells settle before the overflow
reaches the target runs its passes where it ran them before.

What changes beyond the pass, and what is left:

- A pass that ended a wait at the target and reverted sends the
  placement down from the snapshot again and, if the cells are still
  moving at the routability gate then, down to the target once more
  before the next pass. The passes are bounded as before by RouteBase:
  the congestion target, no improvement, the density limit, the
  inflation budget (GPL-0097) and the revert limit.
- Only the iterations from the snapshot down to the routability gate
  extend the iteration limit. Each descent from the gate to the target
  counts against it, so a design that converged near its limit with no
  pass can now stop at GPL-1010 above the target.
- The timing-driven iterations are keyed to overflow thresholds that
  are each used once (64 and 20 percent by default). A pass after the
  last of them, which a wait ended at the target always is with the
  default thresholds and target, is followed by a descent without one.
  That is so today for a wait that closes below the last threshold.
- A routability-driven run that is already at or below the target on
  its first iteration, as a placement that starts from a placed design
  can be, opens the wait and ends it on that iteration: GPL-0099, then
  GPL-0124 after 0 extra iterations. It runs the pass where it
  converged with none before.
- A wait can still end with no pass: when the placement ends for
  another reason, the iteration limit (GPL-1010), a divergence that
  stops it (GPL-0997, GPL-0307) or an invalid gradient or step
  (GPL-0306, GPL-0305); when it converges with no routability snapshot
  saved, which takes a snapshot overflow set below the target
  overflow; and when a divergence recovery (GPL-0112) goes back to the
  snapshot, after which the wait opens again.
- With several regions, a region that converges before its cells settle
  keeps its last displacement ratio, and the settle test asks every
  region. No later wait settles then, and every later pass comes from a
  wait ended at the target (GPL-0124). Before, such a run had no
  further passes at all.
- A region that reaches the target before the others is locked by
  checkConvergence() as before.

Two tests drive the real controller in the main loop's order:
routabilitySnapshot(), runRoutability(), isConverged().
TimingRepairIntegrationTest.OpenSettleWaitStillRunsRoutabilityAtTargetOverflow:
the wait opens at the routability gate with the cells at their peak
displacement. The average at the target with a region still above it
leaves the wait open; the fixture's one region stands in for that
region, and no test has two, so none tells every region from the
first. With every region at the target and the cells still moving,
without the change the pass count stays 0 and the placement converges;
with it the pass runs, inflates and reverts, and the placement goes on.
TimingRepairIntegrationTest.OpenSettleWaitWithoutSnapshotDoesNotRunRoutability:
with a snapshot overflow below the target no snapshot is taken, the
wait stays open at the target and the placement converges with no pass.
It holds without the change too; it pins the snapshot term of the new
condition.

Of the other tests,
PowerDrivenPlacement.WorksWithTimingAndRoutabilityDriven expects a pass
and keeps it: up to a run's first pass nothing changes. No compared
regression golden prints GPL-0099: simple01-rd to simple04-rd run one
pass with no wait, so none changes. upf_aes, place_ios_rd and
congestion_inflation_default are the pass/fail tests that run
routability-driven placement; the metrics-checked flow tests
(test/flow.tcl) run it too and were not run.

Carried in bazel-orfs, not upstreamed; retires with the //:bump onto an
OpenROAD that has it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Øyvind Harboe <oyvind.harboe@zylin.com>
---
 src/gpl/src/nesterovPlace.cpp                 | 55 +++++++++---
 src/gpl/src/nesterovPlace.h                   |  3 +
 .../test/congestion_buffers_timing_test.cpp   | 86 +++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 132 insertions(+), 12 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/gpl/src/nesterovPlace.cpp b/src/gpl/src/nesterovPlace.cpp
index f893ad2..1160ef6 100644
--- a/src/gpl/src/nesterovPlace.cpp
+++ b/src/gpl/src/nesterovPlace.cpp
@@ -938,8 +938,10 @@ void NesterovPlace::runRoutability(int iter,
   // placement that no longer exists by the time it lands. Wait for the motion
   // to come off its peak as well.
   //
-  // This can only ever delay the trigger, so a design already settled at its
-  // overflow gate is unaffected.
+  // The wait only ever delays the pass: a design already settled at its
+  // overflow gate runs it there. Reaching the target overflow does not cancel
+  // a waiting pass either: a wait still open on the iteration the placement
+  // would converge ends there, and the pass runs on that placement.
   const bool is_routability_active
       = npVars_.routability_driven_mode && is_routability_need_
         && average_overflow_unscaled_ <= npVars_.routability_end_overflow;
@@ -961,17 +963,36 @@ void NesterovPlace::runRoutability(int iter,
                NesterovBase::getSettleFraction() * 100.0f);
   }
 
-  if (is_routability_settled) {
+  // A pass can only revert to a saved snapshot, hence the third term.
+  const bool is_wait_ended_by_convergence
+      = is_routability_active && !is_routability_settled
+        && is_routability_snapshot_saved_ && isConvergenceDue();
+
+  if (is_routability_settled || is_wait_ended_by_convergence) {
     if (routability_settle_wait_start_iter_ != -1) {
-      log_->info(GPL,
-                 103,
-                 "Routability end extension finished at iter = {} after {} "
-                 "extra iterations: overflow {:.4f}, cells moving at {:.0f}% "
-                 "of peak displacement.",
-                 iter + 1,
-                 iter - routability_settle_wait_start_iter_,
-                 average_overflow_unscaled_,
-                 getWorstSettleRatio() * 100.0f);
+      if (is_routability_settled) {
+        log_->info(GPL,
+                   103,
+                   "Routability end extension finished at iter = {} after {} "
+                   "extra iterations: overflow {:.4f}, cells moving at {:.0f}% "
+                   "of peak displacement.",
+                   iter + 1,
+                   iter - routability_settle_wait_start_iter_,
+                   average_overflow_unscaled_,
+                   getWorstSettleRatio() * 100.0f);
+      } else {
+        log_->info(GPL,
+                   124,
+                   "Routability end extension ended at iter = {} after {} "
+                   "extra iterations: overflow {:.4f} reached the target "
+                   "overflow {:.4f} before the cells settled, at {:.0f}% of "
+                   "peak displacement.",
+                   iter + 1,
+                   iter - routability_settle_wait_start_iter_,
+                   average_overflow_unscaled_,
+                   npVars_.targetOverflow,
+                   getWorstSettleRatio() * 100.0f);
+      }
       routability_settle_wait_start_iter_ = -1;
     }
 
@@ -1136,6 +1157,16 @@ bool NesterovPlace::isConverged(int gpl_iter_count,
   return false;
 }
 
+bool NesterovPlace::isConvergenceDue() const
+{
+  for (const auto& nb : nbVec_) {
+    if (!nb->isConvergenceDue()) {
+      return false;
+    }
+  }
+  return true;
+}
+
 NesterovBase* NesterovPlace::getTopLevelNB() const
 {
   if (nbVec_.empty()) {
diff --git a/src/gpl/src/nesterovPlace.h b/src/gpl/src/nesterovPlace.h
index 76c0ba8..3bd6488 100644
--- a/src/gpl/src/nesterovPlace.h
+++ b/src/gpl/src/nesterovPlace.h
@@ -153,6 +153,9 @@ class NesterovPlace
   float getWorstSettleRatio() const;
 
   bool isConverged(int gpl_iter_count, int routability_gpl_iter_count);
+  // True when isConverged() would end the placement on this iteration; no
+  // side effects.
+  bool isConvergenceDue() const;
   // Re-derives densityPenalty_ for every region via
   // NesterovBase::updateDensityPenaltyFromRatio() - the same formula
   // NesterovBase::initDensity2() uses at true init, just re-triggered
diff --git a/src/gpl/test/congestion_buffers_timing_test.cpp b/src/gpl/test/congestion_buffers_timing_test.cpp
index ab4d7ed..58dacc5 100644
--- a/src/gpl/test/congestion_buffers_timing_test.cpp
+++ b/src/gpl/test/congestion_buffers_timing_test.cpp
@@ -288,6 +288,15 @@ class TimingRepairIntegrationTest : public tst::IntegratedFixture
     }
   }
 
+  // Sets only the regions' overflow, leaving their average: with several
+  // regions, one can be above the target when the average is at it.
+  void setRegionOverflow(float overflow)
+  {
+    for (const auto& nb : nb_vec_) {
+      nb->sum_overflow_unscaled_ = overflow;
+    }
+  }
+
   // Cells moving at the given fraction of their peak displacement.
   void setDisplacementRatio(float ratio)
   {
@@ -306,6 +315,10 @@ class TimingRepairIntegrationTest : public tst::IntegratedFixture
     ASSERT_TRUE(np_->is_routability_snapshot_saved_);
   }
 
+  bool routabilitySnapshotSaved() const
+  {
+    return np_->is_routability_snapshot_saved_;
+  }
   bool placementSettled() const { return np_->isPlacementSettled(); }
   // True when the last RUDY average, computed by a pass or at convergence, is
   // below the congestion target. A pass that finds it so does not revert.
@@ -539,6 +552,79 @@ TEST_F(TimingRepairIntegrationTest,
       << "a measured placement at the target overflow must converge";
 }
 
+// The settle wait holds the routability pass back while the cells are still
+// moving. Reaching the target overflow must not cancel the pass: a wait still
+// open on the iteration the placement would converge ends there, and the pass
+// runs on that placement.
+TEST_F(TimingRepairIntegrationTest,
+       OpenSettleWaitStillRunsRoutabilityAtTargetOverflow)
+{
+  makePlacer();
+  float current_a = 1.0f;
+  ASSERT_NO_FATAL_FAILURE(saveRoutabilitySnapshot(current_a));
+
+  // Through the routability gate with the cells at their peak displacement:
+  // the pass waits.
+  setDisplacementRatio(1.0f);
+  setOverflow(options_.routabilityCheckOverflow);
+  ASSERT_FALSE(placementSettled());
+  ASSERT_FALSE(runRoutabilityThenConvergence(1, current_a));
+  ASSERT_EQ(ordinary_iterations_, 0);
+  ASSERT_EQ(settleWaitStart(), 1);
+
+  // The average at the target with a region still above it is not
+  // convergence, which takes every region: the wait stays open. The fixture's
+  // one region stands in for the region above the target.
+  setOverflow(options_.overflow);
+  setRegionOverflow(1.5f * options_.overflow);
+  ASSERT_FALSE(runRoutabilityThenConvergence(2, current_a));
+  ASSERT_EQ(ordinary_iterations_, 0)
+      << "the wait must not end before every region is at the target";
+  ASSERT_EQ(settleWaitStart(), 1);
+
+  // Still moving when every region reaches the target: the iteration the main
+  // loop would end the placement on.
+  setOverflow(options_.overflow);
+  ASSERT_FALSE(placementSettled());
+  const bool converged = runRoutabilityThenConvergence(3, current_a);
+  ASSERT_EQ(ordinary_iterations_, 1)
+      << "reaching the target overflow must not cancel the waiting pass";
+  EXPECT_EQ(settleWaitStart(), -1);
+  // The fixture's wire width makes a pass find congestion, so this one
+  // inflated cells and went back to the snapshot, which has yet to be placed.
+  ASSERT_TRUE(routabilityNeeded());
+  ASSERT_GT(rb_->getTotalInflation(), 0);
+  EXPECT_FALSE(converged)
+      << "the placement must not end on the iteration of a pass that reverted";
+}
+
+// A pass that finds congestion goes back to the routability snapshot, so a
+// wait is only ended at the target overflow when there is one. Without a
+// snapshot the wait stays open and the placement converges with no pass.
+TEST_F(TimingRepairIntegrationTest,
+       OpenSettleWaitWithoutSnapshotDoesNotRunRoutability)
+{
+  // A snapshot overflow below the target overflow: no snapshot is taken.
+  options_.routabilitySnapshotOverflow = 0.5f * options_.overflow;
+  makePlacer();
+  float current_a = 1.0f;
+
+  setDisplacementRatio(1.0f);
+  setOverflow(options_.routabilityCheckOverflow);
+  ASSERT_FALSE(runRoutabilityThenConvergence(1, current_a));
+  ASSERT_EQ(ordinary_iterations_, 0);
+  ASSERT_EQ(settleWaitStart(), 1);
+
+  setOverflow(options_.overflow);
+  ASSERT_FALSE(placementSettled());
+  const bool converged = runRoutabilityThenConvergence(2, current_a);
+  ASSERT_FALSE(routabilitySnapshotSaved());
+  EXPECT_EQ(ordinary_iterations_, 0)
+      << "a pass with no snapshot to go back to must not run";
+  EXPECT_EQ(settleWaitStart(), 1);
+  EXPECT_TRUE(converged);
+}
+
 TEST_F(TimingRepairIntegrationTest,
        SynchronousCallbacksPrecedeInflationAndOptimizerInitialization)
 {
